1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,524
Somewhere in the North Sea,

2
00:00:02,524 --> 00:00:05,000
a platform pumps oil from beneath the

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,110
seabed.

4
00:00:06,110 --> 00:00:08,010
The money it earns ends up in

5
00:00:08,010 --> 00:00:10,386
one of the largest investment funds on

6
00:00:10,386 --> 00:00:11,223
Earth.

7
00:00:11,483 --> 00:00:14,263
Norway's oil fund was worth about 2.1

8
00:00:14,263 --> 00:00:16,672
trillion dollars at the end of September

9
00:00:16,672 --> 00:00:18,673
2026.

10
00:00:19,013 --> 00:00:21,086
Divide that by every person in the

11
00:00:21,086 --> 00:00:21,633
country,

12
00:00:21,633 --> 00:00:25,139
and it comes to about 375,000 dollars

13
00:00:25,139 --> 00:00:25,928
each.

14
00:00:26,183 --> 00:00:27,112
Through that fund,

15
00:00:27,112 --> 00:00:30,613
Norway owns on average 1.5 percent of

16
00:00:30,613 --> 00:00:33,833
every listed company in the world.

17
00:00:33,993 --> 00:00:36,950
7,201 companies,

18
00:00:36,950 --> 00:00:39,330
in 68 countries.

19
00:00:39,583 --> 00:00:42,213
Plenty of countries have found oil.

20
00:00:42,463 --> 00:00:44,833
Few have ended up like this.

21
00:00:45,003 --> 00:00:48,093
So what did Norway do differently?

22
00:00:48,413 --> 00:00:51,349
This is The Hidden Economics.

23
00:00:56,983 --> 00:00:58,471
Before the oil,

24
00:00:58,471 --> 00:01:01,205
Norway lived from the sea and the

25
00:01:01,205 --> 00:01:02,343
mountains.

26
00:01:02,343 --> 00:01:04,773
Fishing boats worked the coast.

27
00:01:04,983 --> 00:01:07,604
By the nineteen-fifties its merchant fleet

28
00:01:07,604 --> 00:01:09,986
was described as the third largest in

29
00:01:09,986 --> 00:01:11,063
the world.

30
00:01:11,433 --> 00:01:13,831
And In 1905,

31
00:01:13,831 --> 00:01:16,925
Norsk Hydro began turning waterfalls into

32
00:01:16,925 --> 00:01:18,557
fertiliser.

33
00:01:18,817 --> 00:01:20,062
It was a modest,

34
00:01:20,062 --> 00:01:21,728
hard-working economy,

35
00:01:21,728 --> 00:01:24,227
but not an especially rich one.

36
00:01:24,387 --> 00:01:26,380
In 1970,

37
00:01:26,380 --> 00:01:29,262
Norway's income per person was only about

38
00:01:29,262 --> 00:01:30,679
four-fifths of Sweden's,

39
00:01:30,679 --> 00:01:32,720
and behind Denmark's too.

40
00:01:38,383 --> 00:01:41,551
Few believed there was oil under Norway's

41
00:01:41,551 --> 00:01:43,303
seabed at all.

42
00:01:43,323 --> 00:01:45,068
In 1958,

43
00:01:45,068 --> 00:01:47,592
the national geological survey told the

44
00:01:47,592 --> 00:01:49,274
government the chances could be

45
00:01:49,274 --> 00:01:50,505
discounted.

46
00:01:50,750 --> 00:01:51,362
Still,

47
00:01:51,362 --> 00:01:55,180
Norway claimed its continental shelf.

48
00:01:55,310 --> 00:01:57,298
In 1965,

49
00:01:57,298 --> 00:01:59,455
it agreed a median line through the

50
00:01:59,455 --> 00:02:01,587
North Sea with Britain and Denmark,

51
00:02:01,587 --> 00:02:04,509
and handed out its first 22 production

52
00:02:04,509 --> 00:02:05,828
licences.

53
00:02:06,083 --> 00:02:08,943
The first wells came up dry.

54
00:02:09,203 --> 00:02:09,695
Then,

55
00:02:09,695 --> 00:02:12,883
just before Christmas 1969,

56
00:02:12,883 --> 00:02:16,252
the American company Phillips Petroleum

57
00:02:16,252 --> 00:02:19,443
reported a find called Ekofisk.

58
00:02:19,773 --> 00:02:20,814
At the time,

59
00:02:20,814 --> 00:02:23,216
it was the largest offshore oil field

60
00:02:23,216 --> 00:02:25,418
ever discovered.

61
00:02:25,683 --> 00:02:29,444
Oil started flowing from Ekofisk in June

62
00:02:29,444 --> 00:02:32,233
1971.

63
00:02:32,483 --> 00:02:35,669
Norway had become an oil nation almost

64
00:02:35,669 --> 00:02:37,138
overnight.

65
00:02:42,783 --> 00:02:45,925
Norway's first big decision was about

66
00:02:45,925 --> 00:02:47,153
control.

67
00:02:47,433 --> 00:02:49,587
In 1971,

68
00:02:49,587 --> 00:02:52,415
parliament adopted ten principles,

69
00:02:52,415 --> 00:02:54,984
later called the oil commandments,

70
00:02:54,984 --> 00:02:57,579
to keep the resource under national

71
00:02:57,579 --> 00:03:00,173
control and the industry serving the

72
00:03:00,173 --> 00:03:01,292
country.

73
00:03:01,550 --> 00:03:03,441
In 1972,

74
00:03:03,441 --> 00:03:05,696
it created a state oil company,

75
00:03:05,696 --> 00:03:06,356
Statoil,

76
00:03:06,356 --> 00:03:07,928
and a regulator,

77
00:03:07,928 --> 00:03:10,350
the Petroleum Directorate.

78
00:03:10,890 --> 00:03:12,911
In 1985,

79
00:03:12,911 --> 00:03:15,833
the state also began holding direct stakes

80
00:03:15,833 --> 00:03:17,650
in oil fields itself.

81
00:03:18,180 --> 00:03:21,827
Today the government still owns 67 percent

82
00:03:21,827 --> 00:03:23,733
of Statoil's successor,

83
00:03:23,733 --> 00:03:25,161
Equinor.

84
00:03:25,417 --> 00:03:28,267
The second decision was tax.

85
00:03:28,467 --> 00:03:31,454
Oil companies pay the normal 22 percent

86
00:03:31,454 --> 00:03:32,563
company tax,

87
00:03:32,563 --> 00:03:36,024
plus a special petroleum tax of 71.8

88
00:03:36,024 --> 00:03:37,077
percent.

89
00:03:37,247 --> 00:03:38,079
Together,

90
00:03:38,079 --> 00:03:40,468
the state takes 78 percent of the

91
00:03:40,468 --> 00:03:42,348
profit at the margin.

92
00:03:42,583 --> 00:03:44,530
So the oil pays the state three

93
00:03:44,530 --> 00:03:45,142
ways:

94
00:03:45,142 --> 00:03:47,618
taxes on company profits,

95
00:03:47,618 --> 00:03:49,538
its own share of the fields,

96
00:03:49,538 --> 00:03:52,363
and dividends from Equinor.

97
00:03:58,983 --> 00:04:01,713
Those streams are enormous.

98
00:04:01,713 --> 00:04:03,723
In 2022,

99
00:04:03,723 --> 00:04:05,878
when energy prices spiked,

100
00:04:05,878 --> 00:04:08,299
the state's net cash flow from petroleum

101
00:04:08,299 --> 00:04:12,483
hit a record about 134 billion dollars.

102
00:04:12,633 --> 00:04:14,664
Even in a calmer year like last

103
00:04:14,664 --> 00:04:15,093
year,

104
00:04:15,093 --> 00:04:18,220
it was about 64 billion dollars.

105
00:04:18,483 --> 00:04:21,000
Oil and gas made up 57 percent

106
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:24,207
of the value of everything Norway exported

107
00:04:24,207 --> 00:04:26,633
in 2025.

108
00:04:26,943 --> 00:04:30,517
And through about 8,800 kilometres of

109
00:04:30,517 --> 00:04:31,654
pipelines,

110
00:04:31,654 --> 00:04:34,253
Norway's gas now covers more than 30

111
00:04:34,253 --> 00:04:36,341
percent of all the gas used in

112
00:04:36,341 --> 00:04:39,030
the European Union and Britain.

113
00:04:39,283 --> 00:04:42,752
That much money arriving that fast is

114
00:04:42,752 --> 00:04:44,393
dangerous.

115
00:04:44,623 --> 00:04:46,125
Spend it all at home,

116
00:04:46,125 --> 00:04:48,136
and wages and prices surge,

117
00:04:48,136 --> 00:04:49,639
the currency soars,

118
00:04:49,639 --> 00:04:52,694
and every other industry struggles to

119
00:04:52,694 --> 00:04:53,803
compete.

120
00:04:54,233 --> 00:04:57,602
Economists call it the resource curse.

121
00:05:03,250 --> 00:05:05,542
Norway's answer was to park the money

122
00:05:05,542 --> 00:05:06,600
abroad.

123
00:05:06,710 --> 00:05:08,393
In 1990,

124
00:05:08,393 --> 00:05:10,920
parliament created a petroleum fund.

125
00:05:10,920 --> 00:05:12,928
In May 1996,

126
00:05:12,928 --> 00:05:13,986
the first transfer,

127
00:05:13,986 --> 00:05:16,727
worth about 300 million dollars,

128
00:05:16,727 --> 00:05:17,759
went in.

129
00:05:18,017 --> 00:05:20,327
Parliament sets the rules.

130
00:05:20,337 --> 00:05:22,457
The finance ministry owns the fund on

131
00:05:22,457 --> 00:05:24,057
the people's behalf.

132
00:05:24,057 --> 00:05:26,098
And the central bank's investment arm,

133
00:05:26,098 --> 00:05:28,222
created In 1998,

134
00:05:28,222 --> 00:05:29,647
manages it.

135
00:05:29,717 --> 00:05:31,430
One rule matters most:

136
00:05:31,430 --> 00:05:33,809
the fund is not allowed to invest

137
00:05:33,809 --> 00:05:35,599
in Norway at all.

138
00:05:35,850 --> 00:05:38,570
Then the money compounded.

139
00:05:38,620 --> 00:05:40,245
Here is the value of the fund

140
00:05:40,245 --> 00:05:41,847
at the end of each year,

141
00:05:41,847 --> 00:05:43,840
in billions of dollars.

142
00:05:44,060 --> 00:05:47,405
The line barely moves in the beginning,

143
00:05:47,405 --> 00:05:48,417
then it climbs,

144
00:05:48,417 --> 00:05:49,169
and climbs,

145
00:05:49,169 --> 00:05:51,325
past two thousand billion.

146
00:05:51,583 --> 00:05:53,953
Here is the surprising part.

147
00:05:53,953 --> 00:05:56,342
According to the fund's manager,

148
00:05:56,342 --> 00:05:58,513
the oil money paid in accounts for

149
00:05:58,513 --> 00:06:01,043
less than half of its value today.

150
00:06:01,413 --> 00:06:03,256
The rest has been earned by the

151
00:06:03,256 --> 00:06:05,238
investments themselves.

152
00:06:10,883 --> 00:06:12,427
Most of the money,

153
00:06:12,427 --> 00:06:14,546
about 72 percent,

154
00:06:14,546 --> 00:06:16,193
is in shares.

155
00:06:16,273 --> 00:06:18,603
Around a quarter is in bonds.

156
00:06:18,663 --> 00:06:20,677
A small slice is in property and

157
00:06:20,677 --> 00:06:23,962
in renewable energy infrastructure.

158
00:06:24,217 --> 00:06:27,297
And it is spread across the planet.

159
00:06:27,417 --> 00:06:28,569
The biggest share,

160
00:06:28,569 --> 00:06:30,731
52.9 percent,

161
00:06:30,731 --> 00:06:33,917
is invested in the United States.

162
00:06:34,137 --> 00:06:37,287
Its largest single holdings are Nvidia,

163
00:06:37,287 --> 00:06:39,622
Apple and Alphabet.

164
00:06:39,883 --> 00:06:41,714
Since it began buying shares,

165
00:06:41,714 --> 00:06:44,262
the fund has returned an average of

166
00:06:44,262 --> 00:06:46,487
6.6 percent a year,

167
00:06:46,487 --> 00:06:50,403
or 4.3 percent after inflation and costs.

168
00:06:50,403 --> 00:06:52,205
But it is not a smooth ride:

169
00:06:52,205 --> 00:06:54,667
it lost minus 23 percent in the

170
00:06:54,667 --> 00:06:55,964
financial crisis,

171
00:06:55,964 --> 00:06:59,992
and minus 14 percent in 2022.

172
00:07:05,650 --> 00:07:08,050
The real secret is a rule about

173
00:07:08,050 --> 00:07:09,100
spending.

174
00:07:09,100 --> 00:07:10,953
Since 2001,

175
00:07:10,953 --> 00:07:13,163
the government may only take out,

176
00:07:13,163 --> 00:07:14,034
over time,

177
00:07:14,034 --> 00:07:16,044
what the fund is expected to earn

178
00:07:16,044 --> 00:07:17,760
after inflation.

179
00:07:17,860 --> 00:07:19,687
That was set at 4 percent,

180
00:07:19,687 --> 00:07:23,296
and cut to 3 percent in 2017.

181
00:07:23,550 --> 00:07:25,302
In the budget for this year,

182
00:07:25,302 --> 00:07:28,230
the government planned to use about 56

183
00:07:28,230 --> 00:07:30,205
billion dollars of oil money,

184
00:07:30,205 --> 00:07:33,400
about 2.8 percent of the fund.

185
00:07:33,670 --> 00:07:36,216
The IMF estimates that money from the

186
00:07:36,216 --> 00:07:38,299
fund now pays for about a quarter

187
00:07:38,299 --> 00:07:40,288
of all public spending.

188
00:07:40,550 --> 00:07:43,770
Spending only the return means the capital

189
00:07:43,770 --> 00:07:45,980
is never used up.

190
00:07:46,080 --> 00:07:48,766
The oil is converted into shares,

191
00:07:48,766 --> 00:07:50,959
bonds and buildings around the world,

192
00:07:50,959 --> 00:07:53,176
and Norwegians who are not yet born

193
00:07:53,176 --> 00:07:55,008
will share in it too.

194
00:07:55,250 --> 00:07:58,220
It also protects the economy at home.

195
00:07:58,280 --> 00:08:00,897
Because spending is tied to the fund,

196
00:08:00,897 --> 00:08:02,721
not to this year's oil price,

197
00:08:02,721 --> 00:08:05,365
the IMF concluded that the rule and

198
00:08:05,365 --> 00:08:08,273
the fund would largely insulate Norway

199
00:08:08,273 --> 00:08:10,724
from a fall in oil revenue.

200
00:08:16,383 --> 00:08:17,613
Oil is still big,

201
00:08:17,613 --> 00:08:20,473
but it is not the whole story.

202
00:08:20,723 --> 00:08:22,864
In 2025,

203
00:08:22,864 --> 00:08:25,444
about four-fifths of Norway's output came

204
00:08:25,444 --> 00:08:27,817
from the mainland economy:

205
00:08:27,817 --> 00:08:29,081
the industries,

206
00:08:29,081 --> 00:08:32,151
services and public sector outside oil,

207
00:08:32,151 --> 00:08:33,783
gas and shipping.

208
00:08:34,017 --> 00:08:37,397
That economy runs on an unusual model.

209
00:08:37,547 --> 00:08:39,847
About half of workers belong to a

210
00:08:39,847 --> 00:08:40,907
union.

211
00:08:41,087 --> 00:08:42,086
In wage talks,

212
00:08:42,086 --> 00:08:43,878
the industries that compete

213
00:08:43,878 --> 00:08:46,669
internationally negotiate first,

214
00:08:46,669 --> 00:08:49,204
and everyone else follows their lead,

215
00:08:49,204 --> 00:08:50,996
so pay keeps in step with what

216
00:08:50,996 --> 00:08:53,133
exporters can afford.

217
00:08:53,383 --> 00:08:55,574
Income is spread evenly,

218
00:08:55,574 --> 00:08:57,283
and trust is high.

219
00:08:57,453 --> 00:08:59,214
In the latest OECD survey,

220
00:08:59,214 --> 00:09:02,156
57 percent of Norwegians said they trusted

221
00:09:02,156 --> 00:09:03,917
their national government,

222
00:09:03,917 --> 00:09:07,013
against 40 percent across the OECD.

223
00:09:07,253 --> 00:09:09,394
Trust makes long-term rules,

224
00:09:09,394 --> 00:09:10,450
like the fund's,

225
00:09:10,450 --> 00:09:12,134
easier to keep.

226
00:09:12,383 --> 00:09:14,573
But there is a warning sign.

227
00:09:14,573 --> 00:09:17,372
The OECD says Norway's productivity growth

228
00:09:17,372 --> 00:09:19,661
is now among the lowest in the

229
00:09:19,661 --> 00:09:20,145
OECD,

230
00:09:20,145 --> 00:09:22,689
and its lead in living standards over

231
00:09:22,689 --> 00:09:25,208
other rich countries has narrowed,

232
00:09:25,208 --> 00:09:29,635
from about 42% to 27% in fifteen

233
00:09:29,635 --> 00:09:30,489
years.

234
00:09:36,150 --> 00:09:39,390
The first risk is the oil price.

235
00:09:39,410 --> 00:09:41,799
After the summer of twenty fourteen,

236
00:09:41,799 --> 00:09:43,552
oil fell to around a third of

237
00:09:43,552 --> 00:09:44,810
its level.

238
00:09:44,930 --> 00:09:48,173
Norway's currency weakened by about 30

239
00:09:48,173 --> 00:09:48,835
percent,

240
00:09:48,835 --> 00:09:52,808
and unemployment rose from 3.6 to 4.7

241
00:09:52,808 --> 00:09:53,865
percent.

242
00:09:54,117 --> 00:09:56,617
The second is time.

243
00:09:56,777 --> 00:09:58,732
More than half of Norway's known oil

244
00:09:58,732 --> 00:09:59,441
and gas,

245
00:09:59,441 --> 00:10:00,932
57 percent,

246
00:10:00,932 --> 00:10:03,487
has already been produced.

247
00:10:03,547 --> 00:10:05,905
Output is forecast to fall by the

248
00:10:05,905 --> 00:10:07,296
end of the decade,

249
00:10:07,296 --> 00:10:09,182
as the world tries to move away

250
00:10:09,182 --> 00:10:10,726
from fossil fuels.

251
00:10:10,983 --> 00:10:13,253
The third is age.

252
00:10:13,373 --> 00:10:15,613
Today there are about three people of

253
00:10:15,613 --> 00:10:18,301
working age for every Norwegian over

254
00:10:18,301 --> 00:10:19,573
sixty-five.

255
00:10:19,723 --> 00:10:21,267
By 2050,

256
00:10:21,267 --> 00:10:23,873
official projections imply about two.

257
00:10:23,873 --> 00:10:26,128
Pensions and care will cost more,

258
00:10:26,128 --> 00:10:29,012
just as oil money starts to shrink.

259
00:10:29,250 --> 00:10:32,393
And the fund itself is exposed to

260
00:10:32,393 --> 00:10:34,250
the world's markets.

261
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:36,828
In the manager's own stress test,

262
00:10:36,828 --> 00:10:40,703
a fragmented world economy could knock 37

263
00:10:40,703 --> 00:10:42,667
percent off its value.

264
00:10:48,317 --> 00:10:51,357
So why is Norway so rich?

265
00:10:51,357 --> 00:10:53,487
Not just because it found oil.

266
00:10:53,557 --> 00:10:55,566
Because of what it decided to do

267
00:10:55,566 --> 00:10:56,367
next.

268
00:10:56,537 --> 00:10:59,017
It kept control of the resource.

269
00:10:59,017 --> 00:11:00,717
It taxed it heavily.

270
00:11:00,867 --> 00:11:02,880
It saved the money abroad,

271
00:11:02,880 --> 00:11:05,289
and it spends only the return.

272
00:11:05,550 --> 00:11:08,290
The oil will run out one day.

273
00:11:08,550 --> 00:11:10,829
The rules are designed so that the

274
00:11:10,829 --> 00:11:12,340
fortune does not.

275
00:11:12,520 --> 00:11:13,746
In the IMF's words,

276
00:11:13,746 --> 00:11:16,749
Norway faces the future from a position

277
00:11:16,749 --> 00:11:17,850
of strength.

278
00:11:17,900 --> 00:11:20,073
This is The Hidden Economics.
